# [DISPATCH](../wg/dispatch.html)

## Summary

The DISPATCH Working Group met during IETF 121. The session was chaired in person by Jim Fenton, with co-chairs Rabbat Mansour and Shuping Peng participating remotely, and Area Director Andrew Newton on site at the podium. 

The chairs presented the [Dispatch Chairs' Slides](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-dispatch-dispatch-chairs-slides-00), reviewing the Note Well, session logistics, and the DISPATCH process. The chairs emphasized that DISPATCH outcomes are recommendations to Area Directors and Working Groups rather than binding mandates, and that DISPATCH is not a prerequisite for bringing work to the IETF.

Five topic proposals were presented and dispatched: persistent URI resolution (LinkID), post-quantum key fragmentation guidelines for constrained networks, updating RFC 4648 (Base encodings), DNS embedded answers, and automated audit report discovery (`audits.json`).

